<!--
  The gear inside the 40x40 Settings control on the HOME header.

  ## This glyph is an addition, and it is the only one

  The frozen file draws no path to `settings` from anywhere - no menu row, no
  button, no tab, and no prototype link of any kind (all 265,954 nodes carry zero
  `prototypeInteractions`). So where Settings is reached from is a product
  decision the frame cannot settle, and it was delegated. See
  docs/SETTINGS-APPEARANCE-3.6.6.md for the options weighed.

  It is deliberately **not** the hidden second 40x40 node in the HOME and ABOUT US
  headers (2393:1670 / 2413:61). That node's geometry decodes to a circle of
  radius ~4.6 centred at (6.5,6.9) plus a contour running to the (18,18) corner
  and closing with three straight segments - a magnifier. It is a search control
  the design switched off, not a settings one, and it stays switched off.

  ## Drawn to the plate the header already has

  Same 40x40 viewport as `ic_profile_entry`, same 16x16 glyph box at x=12,y=12, so
  the inset lives in the artwork and the ImageView carries no padding - the
  contract every control on this plate follows. Colour is `profile_entry_icon`,
  which names the shared circular-control chrome rather than the profile: both
  controls sit on the same plate and must invert together.

  The 24-unit path is placed by a group transform - 24 * (2/3) = 16, translated by
  12 - so the numbers read as the frame's own rather than as re-projected
  coordinates.
-->
